Good game, although the difficulty is absolutely punishing and relies heavily on RNG -- sometimes you'll get lucky and nothing bad happens. Other times, you get shafted with no defense or recourse. Aside from that, a decent game with decent story, and some clever writing. (
)
Graphics can be a bit hard on the eyes, but that's what you get with pixel art. Don't think there's any way to resize the game window, either. Soundtrack is quiet and unobtrusive. Probably worth full price.

In few words - this is the best fighting game on PC, no doubt.
+ Great netcode, you can play online without lags near every match;
+ Big character roster, each character has unique moveset and game tactics;
+ VERY cool soundtrack
+ Game is not so hungry 'bout system requirements;
- Medium-to hard threshold to the game, combo-attacks are not so easy to do;
- It's better to obtain arcade stick to play this game, 'cos it has a 6-button mechanics. Gamepad users can be frustrated about it (keyboard users is more happy);
- You can't choose character's alternative costumes, until you buyed them. Shame on you, Capcom
P.S. Beware of wake-up ultra's~

Well, I can tell you something for sure, this game is worth 4€! If you're a fan of LoTR and Assassins Creed, you'll mostly feel home.
Pros:
- Although it's a game from 2014, it has very good graphics and fluid gameplay;
- Lots of side quests and upgrades to do, which will keep you entertained for hours;
- Free Roam, if you're into that;
- Gollum appears... worth it I tell you.
Cons:
- Storyline can be boring as it's not too complex/deep (kill this, sneak into that..)
It's a good game, I'd give it a 8/10. If you have 5€ to spare, buy it, you won't regret it!

Hard to say if i recommend it or not..
Good sides;
Chill music, Mysterious/fantasy back/foregrounds. Cute & well-invented companion, Main character is so sad,depressing & everything around him is hopeless in his eyes (Which i find funny/entertaining as thats exactly how you feel for most maincharacters in puzzle games, Great story & nice cutscenes, Lots of humor. pile of achivements & you get 4 tradeing cards (not worth much but hey!).
Bad sides;
It took me almost 17 hours of nonstop playing to beat haveing to look at a walkthrough constantly as 70-80% of the puzzles made no sense what so ever (Example combineing a frog to a stick) Finding myself stuck all the time. (I play alot of puzzle games but this ranks up with some of the most frustrateing ones). I also ran into a bug and had to load a save that was 2 hours away before the thing i did mess up (altho i did it right acording to the walkthru). So i'd recommend to save often and always have that 1 far-back, Backup save incase something stops working. Yes sometimes in the beginning of the game there is some cut-off sound/text when someones talking. But didin't notice anything for the rest of the game, Theres also a minor spelling issue (sometimes the character might say (in sound) "I can't reach it!", Altho the text says "I can't reach him!" (example if ur clicking on an rock thats high up somewhere).
Eider way.. I guess i would recommend it if its on sale & get it for the great story and all that, But keep a "guide" close at hand. You will most scertainly need it.. Unless you enjoy ripping your hair out, Then have "fun".

The bugs in this game are impressive. Between the repeating "Space Space Space" and controller support dropping out until a restart, it's kinda hard to tell which one is my favorite. That's a lie. My favorite bug make progression difficult for some people.... So I started playing this with 2 friends and after a few hours, we went to bed having enjoyed the mechanics that make this game challenging. We were eager to get back into it the next night but I had errands to run. So my friends used the game's built in profile system to create a new profile so they could play fresh without me and switch back when I jumped in. Well, that worked fine until they switched back and their crystal count dropped to zero. Thanks to some complaints on the forum, we solved the problem easy and kept playing till we reached the final(?) boss and lost repeatedly.
In case someone else has the same problem, here's a rough explanation of the easy workaround: First, go the data folders on the affected machines for the game and set them to readonly. Then on the master machine(the guy who didn't swap profiles), use HFS webserver to host the master data folder. Then, simply run the following c# code on the effected machines(might need to changes some variables) before you start the game every time. This way, the master machine keeps progressing in the game and the other machines get a copy of that progression before the game starts. Easy as pie!
C# code(I ran it in Linqpad):
string userFolderName = Directory.GetDirectories(@"C:\Program Files (x86)\Steam\userdata\").FirstOrDefault();
string mainDir = userFolderName + @"\249990\";
string profilePath = mainDir + @"\remote\PROFILE_";
string cachedPath = mainDir + @"remotecache.vdf";
bool readOnly = (new FileInfo(profilePath)).IsReadOnly;
("ReadOnly:"+readOnly).Dump();
(new FileInfo(profilePath)).IsReadOnly = false;
(new FileInfo(cachedPath)).IsReadOnly = false;
var profileSplit = File.ReadAllLines(profilePath)[0].Split('*');
string steamId = profileSplit[1];
string steamName = profileSplit[2];
(steamId + ":" + steamName).Dump();
//profileSplit.Dump();
var client = new WebClient();
client.DownloadFile("
client.DownloadFile("
File.Delete(cachedPath);
File.Delete(profilePath);
File.Move(cachedPath+"1",cachedPath);
File.Move(profilePath+"1",profilePath);
var crypt = new System.Security.Cryptography.SHA1CryptoServiceProvider();
var allOldBytes = File.ReadAllBytes(profilePath);
int oldBytesLength = allOldBytes.Length;
var oldSha = String.Join("",crypt.ComputeHash(allOldBytes).Select (x => x.ToString("x2")));
(oldBytesLength + ":" + oldSha).Dump();
var newProfileSplit = File.ReadAllLines(profilePath)[0].Split('*');
string wrongSteamId = newProfileSplit[1];
string wrongSteamName = newProfileSplit[2];
(wrongSteamId + ":" + wrongSteamName).Dump();
string allText = File.ReadAllText(profilePath);
string fixedText = allText.Replace(wrongSteamId, steamId).Replace(wrongSteamName, steamName);
File.WriteAllText(profilePath, fixedText);
var allNewBytes = File.ReadAllBytes(profilePath);
int newBytesLength = allNewBytes.Length;
var newSha = String.Join("",crypt.ComputeHash(allNewBytes).Select (x => x.ToString("x2")));
(newBytesLength + ":" + newSha).Dump();
string allCachedText = File.ReadAllText(cachedPath);
string fixedCachedText = allCachedText.Replace("\""+oldBytesLength, "\""+newBytesLength).Replace(oldSha, newSha);
File.WriteAllText(cachedPath, fixedCachedText);
(new FileInfo(profilePath)).IsReadOnly = readOnly;
(new FileInfo(cachedPath)).IsReadOnly = readOnly;
Jokes aside, it's a fun game but if you hit a rough bug, you might end up rage quitting for good.

