One day, I decided to pop in and play Miscreated. I eventually had enough gear to make it to the airfield base, or so I thought. Was along the coastline when a few men looting the place said "friendly!, don't shoot!" I don't KOS, so I let them live (I only had a bow & arrow but still). They stabbed me in the back. Looting a tower behind them, I heard a gun♥♥♥♥♥♥and new my life was over. I managed to take out one of em before it was too late. I was sad, but not entirely depressed, I didn't have much good loot. I managed to respawn in a town that I had previously looted, and had witnessed a fight in. I decide to make my way back the way I came while looting everything I could. I then found a man who seemed to be friendly. He was geared enouh to have two firearms, and a buzzsaw attatched to a baseball bat. He also had some sort of mask. He was friendly to me, taught me to loot properly, showed me where things would spawn in cars, and helped me with gearing and was determined to help. We geared enough to at least stand formidable (at least he was). We made our way to the airfield and finally arrived and started looting. All was well until we decided to split up to cover more ground. I don't know if he could hear me where he was, but I could hear him a minute ago. I see a man running through with a rifle in hand, no ammo, presumably. I decided to shoot as he was a fresh spawn judging by appearance. I had just found a revolver and 5 bullets, and I spent 4 of those 5 shooting at him. It wasn't until I gave up that I decided to go running for my friend for backup. Suddenly, a man with an axe came from my right flank and hit me once. I was already low, so this put me extremely low. I tried to line up a headshot but missed and hit his chest. I was filled with emotions. Fear, anger at myself for missing, sadness. However, through all that there was one thought that filled my mind: "I never asked his name, or his Steam ID". And like that, I was dead. I had failed my friend, my only friend in the zombie apocalypse. FRIEND, IF YOU'RE READING THIS, PLEASE CONTACT ME. At the time, he said he had about 15 hours on the game, and over 2000 on Rust. If any of you know someone who sounds like him, then let me know. At the time, he had his little brother next to him playing CS:GO. Please, take my advice. If you play this, fly solo. Or, if you're really insistant on playing this with a random add him first. I checked my recent players, but I can't check that many players' profiles to see if they all have Rust and Miscreated with about the same time. I added a few who sound similar, but I have yet to get a response. Thank you for listening to my story. ;-;

